    },
    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\"><span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span><span class=\"time\">30 min</span><span class=\"chip warn\">Medium</span><span class=\"chip accent\">DP &middot; LIS</span><a class=\"chip\" href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/longest-increasing-subsequence/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LC 300</a></div>\n  <h1>Longest Increasing Subsequence</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Insight in one line: for every length L keep only the smallest value an increasing subsequence of length L can end with; that list stays sorted, so each new number either extends it or replaces the first tail &ge; it (lower_bound). O(n log n) time, O(n) space; the O(n&#178;) DP is the stepping stone.</p>\n"
